; Willy's Y index: twice the pixel row of the top of his sprite
;
; Index into the row address table #R$8200 (2 bytes per pixel row), so Y / 2 is the pixel row (0-127)
; and Y / 16 the character row (0-15) of the top of his 16x16 sprite. Standing on the floor of
; character row 15 gives $D0 (pixel row 104, character row 13), the value at a new game. The attribute
; address #R$85D3 is always the cell of row Y / 16 (kept in step by #R$8E9C). Y is unsigned: a rise
; through the top wraps it to $F0 or more and the frame loop leaves the room upwards (#R$94B0, which
; sets $D0 in the new room); a fall past the bottom leaves it downwards (#R$94D2, which sets 0).
; .
; Changed by #R$8DD3 (jump: -8 to +8 per pass; fall: +8 per pass; ramp step: 16 up or down), by the
; rope code #R$91BE (while he holds a rope Y is the rope point's Y index minus $10), by the room exits,
; by #R$87CA and by the death restore from #R$85D7. Read by #R$9637 and #R$95C8 (drawing, with the
; ramp offset added) and by the Master Bedroom guard (#R$9534).
; .
; Observed in the simulator: jump arc and fall steps, see findings F92-F95.
@label=WillyY
g$85CF DEFB $00
